  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: one game lobby icon sprite atlas, exactly FOUR columns by FOUR rows, sixteen independent newly illustrated vintage cartoon objects. Square canvas intended 600x600 pixels with sixteen equal150x150cells. Do NOT draw grid lines or cells. Every whole icon must be centered entirely inside its own cell, isolated with at least10pixels of completely transparent margin all around; no overlap or clipping between cells. Keep the exact reading order below.\nROW1, left to right: (1) a tiny charming wooden store cart-stall with red-and-cream awning and gold details; (2) a red-and-gold wrapped gift box with a big bow; (3) a small ornate brass pocketwatch paired with a little golden chest; (4) a gold recruitment card with a bright five-pointed red star, no letters.\nROW2: (5) a mysterious blue cosmic cartoon face/mask with deep navy features and icy cyan eyes, a little internal blue nebula detail, no enclosing badge; (6) a small golden filing cabinet with visible drawers, playful steampunk details; (7) an ivory-paper flight log notebook with green-brown binding and a short pencil; (8) a rounded brown aviator helmet with brass goggles.\nROW3: (9) a compact colorful party/event bunch of red and teal balloons, a ribbon and a few tiny confetti pieces, fully within cell; (10) a purple wizard crystal orb on a tiny brass base with a small wizard hat beside it; (11) a small pilot supply crate with miniature aviator cap/goggles resting on top; (12) a brass winged goggles badge with a teal central lens, no letter or text.\nROW4: (13) a red toy airplane combined with a little golden star medal, compact composition; (14) a green pilot helmet resting in an open green equipment case; (15) a dusty-blue binocular-goggles storage box with two large blue glass lenses; (16) a gold briefcase with one raised five-pointed star on its face and a small handle.\nStyle: cohesive clean 1930s western cartoon game pictograms, medium-bold dark brown ink outlines, rounded playful shapes, warm brass/red/teal/cream colors, simple internal cel shading, tiny controlled highlights. Render enough distinct shape detail to remain recognizable at50pixels. All sixteen are new illustrations, reference-inspired, no exact character identity claims. Genuine transparent alpha background. No scene, no floor, no interface frames, no UI panels, no outer card backplates except the requested card/object itself. Absolutely no words, no labels, no SP letters, no numbers, no logos, no rank marks, no watermark, no exterior drop/cast shadow, no glow. Preserve full transparent gaps between every cell.",
